 "29-inch-display-housing-cnc-machining":{"heroIntro":"A broad display housing with recessed faces, slots and mounting features. Support during machining and measurement is central to planning a similar panel.","setupIntro":"The broad panel rests across the machine table beneath the spindle, with access to the internal face from above. Define actual enclosure dimensions, support points and permitted clamping areas before planning tool reach and operation order for a similar housing.","stepText":["Identify stock, support points and permitted fixture-contact areas. Review support under broad or thin sections, protecting surfaces that affect appearance or fit.","Review access to recesses, slots and edges across the supported panel. Specify flatness and measurement condition, and agree the support arrangement used for acceptance.","Agree flatness, hole positions, mating-edge and cosmetic checks. Locate narrow edge details from mounting datums and mark visible faces, finish, measurement support and dimensions that apply after treatment."],"acceptanceText":["Specify overall dimensions, wall thickness and support areas, with agreed flatness and measurement support for the panel.","Define slot positions, profiles and common datums. Agree methods for checking position and contour.","Specify hole patterns, face relationships, finish and masked interfaces, with final dimensions after treatment and cosmetic acceptance."],"videoWithSetup":true,"omitVisible":true,"compactResources":true,"sequenceNote":false,"setupCaption":"Original workshop photograph · the panel is supported across the machine table. Confirm the support and clamping arrangement for your drawing.","acceptanceHeading":"Check the panel in its agreed support condition"},
 "milling-prismatic-components":{"heroIntro":"Connect bores, pockets and openings to the mounting faces. Plan the locating datums and accessible orientations before confirming a milling route for your drawing.","setupIntro":"Identify locating faces first, then dimension dependent bores and pockets from them. Review holding orientations and any repositioning against the model before quoting.","stepText":["Mark mounting datums and dependent bores or pockets, with stock and clamping restrictions. Give sizes, fits and locations from common datums so hole-to-mounting-face relationships are explicit.","Review tool access in every holding orientation and use the model to decide whether repositioning is needed. Specify flatness, pocket depth, mating surfaces and dimensions affected by treatment.","Define part numbers, drawing revisions and quantities for the actual order. Agree critical-dimensional and positional checks, sampling plan and report format; the photograph contains several forms."],"acceptanceText":["Define critical dimensions and common datums for bores and hole patterns, with the positional measurement method and records.","Define locating faces, pocket depths and mounting interfaces. Agree flatness and dimensional checks.","Define feature relationships across setups, with datum-transfer checks and a sampling plan."],"heroImage":{"id":"multi-feature-milling-operation","crop":true,"alt":"Prismatic components held in vises beneath a milling spindle.","caption":"Real crop from the original workshop photograph · the visible holding and tool access."},"setupImage":{"id":"multi-feature-milling-parts","alt":"Separate block-shaped component forms with machined faces, holes and openings.","caption":"Independent component-form reference. Sampling and dimensional consistency require order-specific measurement records."},"sequenceNote":false,"omitVisible":true,"acceptanceHeading":"Agree bores, mounting faces and cross-setup checks","compactResources":true},
 "milling-a-pocketed-enclosure-form":{"heroIntro":"Pocketed forms combine circular recesses with mounting features. Review wall thickness, tool access and mating interfaces together before machining a similar component.","setupIntro":"Define cavity depth, wall thickness, corner radii and mounting datums together. Review the model for tool access and protected clamping surfaces before confirming the route.","stepText":["Identify clamping faces, pocket depth and minimum wall sections. Check tool reach, internal geometry and radii against the model, including any permitted radius changes. Deep pockets and restricted corners affect access.","Plan pockets, bores and mounting features around agreed datums, with access for tools and clamps. Specify minimum wall thickness and protected areas, and review support while cavities and interfaces are machined.","Agree depth, wall, position and mating-surface checks, including post-finish dimensions. Locate holes and bores from mounting datums and mark seal lands, cosmetic faces and dimensions that apply after treatment."],"acceptanceText":["Specify pocket depth, corner radius, wall thickness and machining allowance. Agree depth and remaining-wall checks from the drawing.","Define datum faces, hole positions and mating interfaces, with position, flatness and sealing-face acceptance.","Define treatment and protected dimensions, with final-dimensional and cosmetic acceptance."],"heroImage":{"id":"milling-enclosure-parts","alt":"Separate pocketed component forms with circular recesses, flat faces and mounting holes.","caption":"Independent component-form reference · a common part or machining sequence with the workshop setup is not established."},"setupCaption":"Real crop from the original workshop photograph. Exact material, cavity depth and wall thickness come from your drawing.","sequenceNote":false,"omitVisible":true,"acceptanceLayout":"table","acceptanceHeading":"Agree cavity, interface and final-finish checks","compactResources":true},
